GRAVEYARD WHOLE-SCENE SOURCE AND PROVENANCE KIT

This compact kit intentionally contains no full upscaled images, large comparisons, previews, runtime/model binaries or intermediate tiles. The untouched native_floor.png is 1536x1024 RGB. Its generation prompt, exact locked style block, metadata and reference roles are included. The requested image-model name was supplied in the prompt; the actual generation backend was not exposed. Reference images are described but not duplicated here.

COMPLETED TEST
Official Real-ESRGAN x4plus anime 6B produced a 6144x4096 AI-upscaled derivative; a 3072x2048 option was derived using Pillow Lanczos. These are upscales, not native high-resolution generations or recovered ground truth. Full results are delivered separately.
One continuous source was processed in 70 computational batches, with 160px cores, 32px context and an extra 16px reflected processing margin. Each batch ran in a fresh process; context was discarded with no blend, preserving single-source geometry. No artwork was artistically stitched.
Total wall time: 193.1008 seconds. Maximum child RSS: 3316116 KiB. Initial larger/long-lived-model attempts were killed; successful process isolation is documented.
Thread setting: 2 threads requested after loading the model, but NCNN reported Winograd convolutions retained the load-time 4-thread setting. OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 was also set. The archived scripts preserve this tested behavior.
Seam checks against independent untiled reference crops: A mean absolute RGB difference 0.0178788/255, max 5/255; B mean 0.0154645/255, max 2/255. No visible seams were observed. AI changes small contours/texture and flattens fills. Raised rocky edging is already present in the native source.

TESTED WORKSPACE RUNTIME
Linux x86_64, Python 3.12.14, NCNN 1.0.20250916 CPU, NumPy 2.3.5, Pillow 12.3.0. No visible GPU. NCNN wheel download was approximately 6.1 MB. Only NCNN was installed; NumPy and Pillow were already available. The small wrapper does not use OpenCV or NCNN model-zoo helpers.

